{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"},"metadata":{"title":"AstronomyKit","externalID":"AstronomyKit","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift bindings for Don Cross’ "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" library."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"AstronomyKit-logo"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit wraps Don Cross’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and exposes the underlying C functionality through idiomatic Swift APIs."}]},{"anchor":"Features","level":3,"text":"Features","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions for the Sun, Moon, planets, and Jupiter’s moons"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ecliptic position and velocity in one call: longitude, latitude, distance, and their rates"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Moon phase angles, quarter searches, illumination, and libration","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sunrise, sunset, moonrise, culmination, and custom altitude searches"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lunar and solar eclipse prediction with timing"}]}]},{"content":[{"inline