 not guaranteed. Event-time calculations can amplify these rounding differences."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For persisted numerical caches, include "},{"code":"AstronomyConfig.ephemerisVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the platform, architecture, OS, and toolchain identity. Review stored positions and event times when upgrading. Numerical regression tolerances are separate from absolute astronomical accuracy limits."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialPositions","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CoordinateSystems","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialBody","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Observer","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Constellation","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Aberration","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/EquatorDate"],"anchor":"Position-Calculations","title":"Position Calculations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonPhases","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Moon","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonPhase","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonQuarter","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Libration","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/LunarNode","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/NodeKind"],"anchor":"Moon","title":"Moon"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/RiseSetTimes","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Eclipses","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/SeasonsAndEvents","doc:\/\/